313 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 54 0 R
/E (Q2. Explain the working principle of YOLO.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
314 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 54 0 R
/E (Answer: YOLO stands for You Only Look Once.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
315 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 54 0 R
/E (It processes the complete image using a deep learning neural network and predicts bounding boxes, class labels and confidence scores. YOLO performs detection in a single main detection process, which makes it suitable for fast object detection.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
316 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 54 0 R
